Z||000021||Haze_Performance||10-27-2001||03:44 AM||||<B>Update:</B><P>Well after much cutting & improvements in plate design, I've come to the decision that the color plates should not be removable. I know how hard it is to take apart the lens. So I will offer one color, that I will install in the lens. If you want to take responsibility (Pulling the lights apart), I will sell the replacement color plates (in other colors) that will directly replace the ones I installed. (You just pull the one out & drop in your new color) I will offer the any color for the original install. (Just a warning... If you pick a other color than red, You might have problems with your local police.)<P>I will have some pics to post soon. I still need to get my PONTIAC mask from a local shop. At that time I will post pics of the PONTIAC script lights in all the available colors.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks for looking<P>-Haze  <P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallindysig_copy.jpg">                 .                 <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallredsig.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red">Classic Fiero Owners - <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> - Pennocks Wild Rides - <A HREF="http://clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||10
Z||000022||Haze_Performance||10-27-2001||04:03 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>Carl--It won't do me any good as I have a fastback, but I think it's a great idea.  (It's also good to know that I'm not the only fool up at odd hours.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I was just thinking... You can take the light-up PONTIAC off your GT & replace it with MONKEY MAN. It wouldn't be that difficult.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallindysig_copy.jpg">                 .                 <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallredsig.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red">Classic Fiero Owners - <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> - Pennocks Wild Rides - <A HREF="http://clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||10
Z||000023||Ferrari_cdn||10-27-2001||05:21 AM||||I might be having three characters, and there is a split between left and right set of lights, in the middle.  If I have three characters, the second one would be in the middle so would that be a problem?||||reg||1
Z||000024||Haze_Performance||10-27-2001||05:38 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ferrari_cdn:<BR><B>I might be having three characters, and there is a split between left and right set of lights, in the middle.  If I have three characters, the second one would be in the middle so would that be a problem?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well........ You can't put a letter in the middle. It wont light-up right. It needs to be on the plastic to work. You can have 2 on the left lens & 1 on the right or vice versa. <P>Sorry  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <P>||||reg||9
